 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "sessions is a list of strings \"<user_id>,<input_tokens>,<output_tokens>,<plan>\" with canonical decimal token counts. pricing is a list of comma-separated plan rows; every plan used by a session has exactly one row. Prices are non-negative integers in an abstract smallest currency unit per token, so every amount is an exact integer. Return [user_id, total] for every user that has at least one session, sorted by user_id in code-point order. Level 3: a pricing row is \"<plan>,<input_price>,<output_price>,<monthly_fee>,<included_tokens>,<usage_cap>\". Usage charges for a (user, plan) pair are computed as in level 2 (free tokens consumed in session order, input before output), then capped: the pair pays monthly_fee + min(usage_cap, usage charges). A user's total is the sum over their plans.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
